#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133597 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133788 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad9f55b2-ce37-507f-8cb6-7d4e30e6868a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector Onto a Subspace"}] :question/id #uuid "b8bbe0e1-8bf1-5b3a-a77e-6350ea77e83f" :question/math-academy-id "e-5575" :question/problem "Verify whether the vectors $\\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2, \\mathbf{a}_3$ are linearly independent, and find the orthogonal projection of $\\mathbf{x}$ onto the subspace spanned by the vectors $\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2, \\mathbf{a}_3 \\},$ where\n![](images/e1/e11a1239e429520c575fed6ac0c9af383ba8ce58b6df8616218998a58c63748c.svg)" :question/worked-solution "First, we verify whether $\\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2, \\mathbf{a}_3$ are linearly independent. So, we start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}↔{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -10 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -15\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{3}{2}){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, the pivot columns correspond to the linearly independent vectors $\\mathbf{a}_1$ and $\\mathbf{a}_2$ that form the basis of our span.\n\nNow, the orthogonal projection of $\\mathbf{x}$ onto the subspace spanned by the linearly independent columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{proj}_{S} \\: \\mathbf{x} = A(A^T\\!A)^{-1}\\!A^T\\,\\mathbf{x}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n![](images/78/7885074c85f490a410f26a1b4d7836134b13a36923b99d31e3b670b8c1dd75f5.svg)\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}26 & 8 \\\\ 8 & 3\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -8 \\\\ -8 & 26\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133598 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133789 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c07721dd-4b97-5d57-8de1-5098117e3071" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector Onto a Plane"}] :question/id #uuid "ac8363a8-fc77-52e0-b060-5e3a45c5171a" :question/math-academy-id "e-5576" :question/problem "Find the orthogonal projection of the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ onto the plane $\\mathbf{r}=s\\mathbf{v}+t\\mathbf{w},$ where $s,t\\in\\mathbb R,$ and\n![](images/c7/c7b322970113e415b78a9cc74469c6cad86404f0929e2091f8c6be2e1329f7bf.svg)" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $\\mathbf v$ and $\\mathbf w$ are linearly independent. \n\nThe orthogonal projection of $\\mathbf{x}$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{proj}_{S} \\: \\mathbf{x} = A\\left(A^T\\!A\\right)^{-1}\\!A^T\\,\\mathbf{x}.\n$$\n\nSince our plane passes through the origin, it defines the subspace $S=\\text{Span}\\{\\mathbf{v}, \\mathbf{w}\\}$ in $\\mathbb{R}^3.$ In our case, we have\n![](images/73/736da2e7e8541700ba158e3b983bc2320427755eb7da3190b62dc743972d083c.svg)\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}12 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 12\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -20\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{32}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -20\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272103 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133788 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad9f55b2-ce37-507f-8cb6-7d4e30e6868a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector Onto a Subspace"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "443359c7-fb89-50aa-b347-e018a824150b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269886} {:answer/id #uuid "77f8db24-b41e-59c8-be15-8e4cbd9af27c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270333} {:answer/id #uuid "7875c178-5636-50d1-bec7-110a07318bd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270338} {:answer/id #uuid "969155b0-4987-59db-9642-2017d4a40120" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270593} {:answer/id #uuid "fa10fca0-76f0-589d-a688-2ee2285fa099" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271455}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7875c178-5636-50d1-bec7-110a07318bd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270338} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c78ed7b-3a00-5ef0-a2ad-6f19136675b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271729}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "80c90161-ef79-5c5d-8635-c87c29b5e681" :question/math-academy-id "q-140473" :question/problem "Find the vector in the subspace spanned by ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ \nthat is closest to the vector $x,$ where \n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly independent. \n\nThe closest vector to $x$ in the subspace spanned by ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace, which is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{30}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388723 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133788 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad9f55b2-ce37-507f-8cb6-7d4e30e6868a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector Onto a Subspace"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c34ca5fe-08f4-5df7-b474-ed822b7bd89b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388725} {:answer/id #uuid "acdf00ba-91a7-5488-8545-026a8d082afb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388726} {:answer/id #uuid "4a195a52-8ce9-5053-b42d-97c4f5710244" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388727} {:answer/id #uuid "edd1123b-b5b1-5929-a337-c49a7db7b5b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388728} {:answer/id #uuid "785e1b0c-75c6-5f36-9833-976480b92739" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388729}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "acdf00ba-91a7-5488-8545-026a8d082afb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388726} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5915291-9a74-5ab8-ac85-36586c0071b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388724}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2c94191a-43a1-5922-ab22-a6d441b65abc" :question/math-academy-id "q-140474" :question/problem "Verify whether the vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}$ are linearly independent, and find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the vectors ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we verify whether ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}$ are linearly independent. So, we start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -9\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -7\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+7{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, the pivot columns correspond to the linearly independent vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ that form the basis of our span.\n\nNow, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the linearly independent columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 11\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{54}[\\begin{aligned}11 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275452 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133788 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad9f55b2-ce37-507f-8cb6-7d4e30e6868a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector Onto a Subspace"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e65fe50-a25e-5d8f-a15e-eb4be1c48ca6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272657} {:answer/id #uuid "40e036b7-b6f5-543d-9dc6-ee62ee075163" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272939} {:answer/id #uuid "903c973b-1b4d-5c8a-8126-7bba89c25430" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273641} {:answer/id #uuid "baa01808-3901-59a9-9b68-5fb51e3cc8fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274005} {:answer/id #uuid "c0e064e3-db1c-534e-84a8-2812db9a5886" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274060}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e65fe50-a25e-5d8f-a15e-eb4be1c48ca6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272657} :answer-field/id #uuid "2610a578-852b-5654-9ba1-b1d74727d205" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274703}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "58326646-892e-5c31-8f2b-b027f89873ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-158124" :question/problem "Find the vector in the subspace spanned by ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ \nthat is closest to the vector $x,$ where \n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly independent. \n\nThe closest vector to $x$ in the subspace spanned by ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace, which is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}34 & -8 \\\\ -8 & 3\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{38}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 8 \\\\ 8 & 34\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381153 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133789 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c07721dd-4b97-5d57-8de1-5098117e3071" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector Onto a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38cb58d9-c219-5cd3-857e-617db708c775" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381155} {:answer/id #uuid "3225a20e-5323-598e-a81d-d85f880917a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381156} {:answer/id #uuid "bfe44d05-813c-5ecb-b916-7c0d6574c9ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381157} {:answer/id #uuid "de168641-2cbe-5bf4-823c-2597e304e780" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381158} {:answer/id #uuid "4336dfeb-2181-52e1-8663-f9713bc181c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381159}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38cb58d9-c219-5cd3-857e-617db708c775" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381155} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c05bf0d-0538-5f74-84b6-1e68c31a2e46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381154}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "679bef56-95dc-516b-b915-5eac172b1256" :question/math-academy-id "q-158298" :question/problem "Find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the plane  $r=sv+tw,$ where $s,t\\in R,$ and\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $v$ and $w$ are linearly independent. \n\nThe orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nSince our plane passes through the origin, it defines the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{v,w}$ in ${R}^{3}.$ In our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ v & w \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 9\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}9 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNotice that we obtained ${\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=x.$ This simply means that $x$ lies in the plane, i.e., \n\n$$\nx\\in \\text{Span}{v,w}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389002 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133789 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c07721dd-4b97-5d57-8de1-5098117e3071" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector Onto a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59df8c83-20c2-59c0-bf86-ff91d435fad5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389004} {:answer/id #uuid "5859b576-61ad-5ce5-a21e-ba9d528365f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389005} {:answer/id #uuid "28fb4c7a-5133-53e0-ba21-c179f97f1979" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389006} {:answer/id #uuid "e56685f2-15d8-5cc1-8330-230a60f3bdc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389007} {:answer/id #uuid "24c325b9-2c1e-539a-94de-23336697b0f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389008}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24c325b9-2c1e-539a-94de-23336697b0f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389008} :answer-field/id #uuid "45ddbeff-2df7-55fa-abb1-f8f4f1b0d152" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389003}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "51493b5e-5437-5dda-a56f-ba4f747b7597" :question/math-academy-id "q-158362" :question/problem "Find the orthogonal projection of the vector $x$ onto the plane $r=sv+tw,$ where $s,t\\in R,$ and\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $v$ and $w$ are linearly independent. \n\nThe orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nSince our plane passes through the origin, it defines the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{v,w}$ in ${R}^{3}.$ In our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ v & w \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}9 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134240 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133789 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c07721dd-4b97-5d57-8de1-5098117e3071" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector Onto a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8560ae62-9640-5782-98b3-7ba5b4600273" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131480} {:answer/id #uuid "b86ff9aa-51d3-5194-a6b0-69a920e89496" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131481} {:answer/id #uuid "e618595b-5184-5224-b0e0-b817868bb370" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131482} {:answer/id #uuid "f5bdb7a4-47a2-5962-96ad-1f392d0f4629" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131483} {:answer/id #uuid "6caa0167-0f6d-5b4b-8567-c2068db5459b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131484}] :answer-field/id #uuid "329c924a-91aa-5408-994b-245b1a09eed1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131479}] :question/id #uuid "848f3ad4-bc09-5a10-9032-79f56e1beebe" :question/math-academy-id "q-39857" :question/problem "Find the orthogonal projection of the vector $x$ onto the plane $r = sv + tw$, where $s, t ∈ R$, and\n$v = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}, w = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}, x = \\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134296 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133788 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad9f55b2-ce37-507f-8cb6-7d4e30e6868a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector Onto a Subspace"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "558dcadf-8fa9-5fe6-90d1-482ebeb3ffd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324682} {:answer/id #uuid "8a71d7e2-5028-5970-ab26-0684ce90dd62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325149} {:answer/id #uuid "c2c1a191-4f44-5e7d-b99a-12c121cef867" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325646} {:answer/id #uuid "ebd22a2e-9570-55de-8252-8f1ba96b468f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326047} {:answer/id #uuid "eec88fa8-4e28-5096-b9b5-8eabd09d16ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326078}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eec88fa8-4e28-5096-b9b5-8eabd09d16ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326078} :answer-field/id #uuid "029047ee-8771-59d2-81f5-3036fece528e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326224}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "22c16d4d-ef3b-582d-a66e-91e72ba35f45" :question/math-academy-id "q-40570" :question/problem "Find the vector in the subspace spanned by ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ \nthat is closest to the vector $x,$ where \n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly independent. \n\nThe closest vector to $x$ in the subspace spanned by ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace, which is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 12\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}6 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326855 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133789 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c07721dd-4b97-5d57-8de1-5098117e3071" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector Onto a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21558261-3635-532d-bf86-0b99ceb5135b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324247} {:answer/id #uuid "32e5c908-2d0c-576f-a7fc-063595179258" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324379} {:answer/id #uuid "4b7f1fcd-da29-5b94-a7cb-6473a47e3f23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324586} {:answer/id #uuid "86aed970-10f2-5a12-a0b3-85e338b1cf37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325117} {:answer/id #uuid "f6e4087a-df75-507a-a69e-ddd45ea92c1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326146}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86aed970-10f2-5a12-a0b3-85e338b1cf37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325117} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ddc99c8-8006-5285-b9c8-bf65ce032b26" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326299}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0c985ebf-e974-5d23-b225-4f6255e4f5ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-40573" :question/problem "Find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the plane  $r=sv+tw,$ where $s,t\\in R,$ and\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $v$ and $w$ are linearly independent. \n\nThe orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nSince our plane passes through the origin, it defines the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{v,w}$ in ${R}^{3}.$ In our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ v & w \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}9 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394518 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133789 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c07721dd-4b97-5d57-8de1-5098117e3071" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector Onto a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a855dd7f-2964-58f3-aef5-397b1b316183" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394520} {:answer/id #uuid "927d2699-661e-58df-8757-2eaad2d7bc64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394521} {:answer/id #uuid "11f17b72-0d4d-5f62-97b8-429cc8c3a8b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394522} {:answer/id #uuid "e0738560-1ba7-58a5-86f2-a975f9353566" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394523} {:answer/id #uuid "3cde2fa1-b566-513c-a5a0-3c64abe2ab15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394524}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "927d2699-661e-58df-8757-2eaad2d7bc64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394521} :answer-field/id #uuid "79066dd9-37e4-5335-842f-84b855bcfbfe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394519}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f07d051f-511e-591e-9291-2d697e2bdb0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-83581" :question/problem "Find the orthogonal projection of the vector $x$ onto the plane $r=sv+tw,$ where $s,t\\in R,$ and\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $v$ and $w$ are linearly independent. \n\nThe orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nSince our plane passes through the origin, it defines the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{v,w}$ in ${R}^{3}.$ In our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ v & w \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 14\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}7 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382580 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133788 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad9f55b2-ce37-507f-8cb6-7d4e30e6868a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector Onto a Subspace"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "843b36fc-a979-5d98-9172-f5a5e36f6eeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382582} {:answer/id #uuid "8c4c364f-8b3a-59b9-a62e-1632ec0c6c9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382583} {:answer/id #uuid "6f2f6a7d-f3f7-59c9-83c7-88653f472779" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382584} {:answer/id #uuid "e70b3f15-2b72-556d-8d3d-7217fc758d42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382585} {:answer/id #uuid "de07c50e-35f1-5988-87f3-73d189220c4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382586}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de07c50e-35f1-5988-87f3-73d189220c4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382586} :answer-field/id #uuid "240379d3-c0ac-56d8-a1b8-814d27c2a6bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382581}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "81d378b2-231c-5d07-922f-4a8c686008d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-86821" :question/problem "Verify whether the vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}$ are linearly independent, and find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the vectors ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,4 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we verify whether ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}$ are linearly independent. So, we start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, the pivot columns correspond to the linearly independent vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ that form the basis of our span.\n\nNow, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the linearly independent columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,4 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 \\\\ -6 & 14\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -26\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}14 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -26\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
